  "task": {
    "objective": "Bring all three crew members to x>=6 across two channels using four reusable parts and temporary spans.",
    "natural_termination": "All crew physically occupy far-bank ground simultaneously; otherwise truncate at tick 144. A previously arrived crew member may return to help, and arrival reward is not repeated.",
    "interaction": "Mass equals one plus carried part count. Unbraced spans carry mass one; braced spans carry mass two. The builder consumes a held part to install a span, the stabilizer sustains it, and the porter cannot cross while holding two parts. Consent-based handoffs and bridge recovery move exactly existing material identities.",
    "observation_access": "Map, roles, all part locations and owners, bridge support/lifetime/capacity and current crew locations are public. The acting role receives its identity one-hot. There are no private fields.",
    "transition_order": "Movement uses existing spans/capacities and rotating mass arbitration; pickup/drop and consent-based handoffs follow; support decays or is renewed; the builder installs or retrieves a span; unsupported lifetime decays; overload/expiry collapses return parts and affected crew to the western bank; arrivals and termination follow."
  },
  "invariant_notes": [
    "Every part identity has exactly one owner status: ground -1, a carrier 0..2, or an installed socket 3..6.",
    "There is at most one installed part per socket; material_total is always four.",
    "Carrier loads respect pickup/handoff capacities [0,1,2]; a porter with two parts has mass three and cannot enter any bridge.",
    "Support lies in [0,10], lifetime in [0,12]; built flags are derived from actual part ownership.",
    "Agents may share land. On a surviving bridge, final total occupant mass is at most capacity.",
    "Collapse recovery is an explicit game rule, not a claim about realistic engineering; it conserves all parts and preserves negative consequences.",
    "The far-bank first-arrival flags are monotone, but natural termination requires current positions.",
    "Raw terminal state is absorbing and does not award another arrival or completion bonus."
  ]
